course: dictionary
lesson: 3328
title: Event: something that happens
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An event is something that happens. It can be small, like the bell ringing for lunch, or big and important or unusual. The word can also mean a planned occasion, like a party or a concert.
explain: Look at the words around it to find which meaning fits. «A miracle is an amazing event that Christians believe shows God's power at work» tells you the event was unusual and important. «The events are put in order on a timeline» tells you they are things that happened, in the order they happened.
explain: Sports day gives another clue. Each race is an event: the sack race, the long jump and the 100 metres are all events. So when the sentence mentions a race or competition in a sports programme, event means one of those races.
fact: An event is something that happens, especially something important or unusual.
fact: An event can be a planned occasion, like a party, concert or sports day.
fact: In a sports programme, an event is one race or competition, like the 100 metres.
fact: On a timeline, events are shown in the order they happened, with equal steps for equal numbers of years.
fact: «In the event of» means if something happens, and «main event» means the most important part of something.
exercise: «A miracle is an amazing event that Christians believe shows God's power at work.» What does event mean here? | *Something important or unusual that happens | A race in a sports programme | A bell that rings for lunch | A bag of sweets
exercise: «The sack race and the long jump are both events on sports day.» What is an event here? | A line showing years in order | *One race or competition in a sports programme | A planned menu for lunch | Something amazing that happens
exercise: What does «in the event of» mean? «In the event of rain, we will stay inside.» | Without any reason | Only once | *If something happens | At the same time as
test: «The party was the main event of the year.» What does main event mean? | *The most important thing that happened | A race on sports day | A small thing that nobody noticed | A bag of party food
test: «A sequence of events» is a set of things that happen in order. What does sequence mean here? | A colour of paint | *The order things happen in | A kind of sports race | A loud noise
exam: «A timeline shows events in the order they happened, with equal steps for equal numbers of years.» Which meaning of event fits? | A planned party with food | One race in a sports programme | *Things that happen, in order | Something important or unusual
